      "body": "The handler performs a non-atomic existence check (SELECT for a matching userId/link) and then, when nothing is found, continues to fetch metadata and insert a new row (line 136 onward). Two concurrent requests for the same previously-unsaved link can both observe no existing row and both insert, creating duplicate content records and duplicate processing jobs. The check must be made atomic with the write (e.g., a unique constraint on (userId, link) with upsert/conflict handling, or a transaction with locking) to prevent duplication.",
